# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# The caret goes everywhere.  A file of forty numbered lines is opened
# and the caret is walked by every key an editor answers -- Home, End,
# Up, Down, Left, Right, PgUp -- each move proven where it can only be
# proven, by typing a mark and reading back WHERE in the file it
# landed.  Then the page follows: a click puts the caret under the
# pointer, and a caret sent off the top brings the view up to meet it.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Development
wait 4
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 150
expect-title Project
note the project is opened by the shell's own panel, its description
note picked where the panel first stands
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
expect-title Open
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
expect-no-title Open
note a file opens into an editor of its own; the caret stands at the
note END of the last line, where a person left off writing
click-window Project
wait 8
key Down
wait 8
key Return
wait 90
expect-title main.bas
note HOME takes the caret to the head of the line it is on
key Home
wait 3
key q
wait 6
note UP lifts it to the line above -- proven by a mark that can only
note land there if the caret left the bottom line
key Up
wait 3
key Home
wait 3
key w
wait 6
note DOWN returns it, RIGHT walks it into the line, and the marks
note spell out the road the caret took
key Down
wait 3
key Home
wait 3
key e
wait 6
key Home
wait 3
key Right
key Right
key Right
wait 3
key t
wait 6
note DELETE takes the character the caret is BEFORE, not behind
key Delete
wait 6
note END runs to the tail, where typing appends
key End
wait 3
key n
wait 6
note the whole road, saved and read back
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas w390 line39
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas eq4t0 line40n
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/main.bas eq4t00
note the caret sent above the page brings the page UP to meet it, so
note it is never lost off the top edge: two pages up land it on the
note first line, and the view has come up to show that line
key Prior
wait 4
key Prior
wait 4
key Prior
wait 8
expect-pixel 253 322 000000
note with the page at its top, a click lands the caret on the line
note under the pointer at its first column -- the third line here
click 194 356
wait 6
key k
wait 6
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas k30 line03
quit
